# ── Build / generated artifacts that we DO commit ────────────────────────────
# gen/go is intentionally committed — it is the protobuf contract surface
# consumed by all Go modules in the workspace.

apps/dashboard/.next/
.claude/
.gocache/
.codex-tmp/
.playwright-cli/

# macOS file-sync conflict copies ("pmsjwt 2.go", "page 3.tsx").
# In Go these are fatal rather than untidy: every .go file in a directory is
# compiled, so a duplicate is a redeclaration error for every symbol in it.
# Ignoring them keeps a sync race from being committed; it does not stop the
# race, which is what moving this repo out of a synced folder would do.
* [0-9].go
* [0-9].sql
* [0-9].ts
* [0-9].tsx
* [0-9].mod
* [0-9].sum
